          "description": "An absolute path in the node's Mutable File System (MFS). Paths under /ipfs/, /ipns/ and /ipld/ are rejected: the daemon would resolve them as content paths, letting a closed-world MFS tool read from the network. Copy content into MFS with mfs_cp, whose source is an MfsCopySource. A segment equal to . or .. is rejected, and so is an empty first segment (//): path cleaning would otherwise turn /a/../ipns/x or //ipfs/x into a content path (R13 security L2). Bare /ipfs, /ipns and /ipld name ordinary MFS entries."
